# AUR packages, installed via yay by the [packages] group on Arch machines
# (skipped entirely on apt machines — add Debian equivalents to apt.list or a
# TODO in install.sh if one of these is ever needed there).
#
# google-chrome deliberately NOT here: install it with `omarchy install browser
# chrome` instead (bootstrap README, per-machine ceremonies). The bare AUR
# package skips Omarchy's browser setup — /etc/opt/chrome/policies/managed
# (theme colors never apply and can't be set manually), ~/.config/chrome-flags.conf
# (native Wayland + gnome-libsecret password store), and the copy-url/yt-dlp hosts.
# leaf: terminal Markdown previewer (github.com/RivoLink/leaf) — `leaf README.md` (-bin: prebuilt, no Rust toolchain)
leaf-markdown-viewer-bin
